{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_plan", "label": "loom \u2014 Graph Runtime Implementation Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eleven TDD tasks: graph math, the generator/interpreter, seed graphs, the loopback server, the editor, hash-locked DoD checks, resume, SKILL.md wiring and tier-2 evals. Every task ends with a green test-loom.cjs."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_graph_core", "label": "graph-core.mjs \u2014 single source of graph math", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pure and dependency-free so it can run in three hosts: inlined as source into the conductor (which forbids require/import), imported by graph-server.mjs, and imported by the browser editor. The test net asserts the inlined copy is byte-identical to the module minus its final export line, so no second implementation can exist."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_scaffold_loom", "label": "scaffold-loom.cjs \u2014 generator emitting the interpreter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Emits a ~60-line interpreter loop over a graph spliced in as DATA; it only emits text, never reaches into the server's or editor's job."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_test_loom", "label": "test-loom.cjs \u2014 agent-free regression net", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Agent-free by construction \u2014 every assertion is pure graph math, generator output or file I/O \u2014 so the safety heart of the design is testable without spawning a subagent. Loads the ESM core by dynamic import inside main() so the suite stays a single node invocation."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_dominance_by_deletion", "label": "dominates() is proof by deletion, with no heuristics on top", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Do not restrict it to immediate predecessors of the target: a gate two hops from the terminal (Review -> DoDGate -> PR) dominates just as strongly, and such a restriction makes every multi-hop gate report a false violation. Dominance is a property of the graph, never of execution history \u2014 'already passed' is expressed by leaving the gate out of unsatisfiedGates at the call site."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_predicates_fail_closed", "label": "Unknown predicate operators fail closed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An unrecognised operator must not silently open a path, and a null result must not throw; matches() returns false for anything it does not understand."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_non_passing_edge_rule", "label": "Only a gate's LOCKED passing edge may lead onward", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dominance proves a gate is VISITED, not SATISFIED: DoDGate --fail--> Done leaves the gate on every path and still reaches the terminal. The rule must cover every non-passing edge \u2014 an appended when:'always' edge is the same bypass in different clothing and also defeats the interpreter's hard-fail because pickEdge never returns null. Testing eq===true alone checks the predicate's VALUE and not its FIELD, so a minted {field:'anythingAtAll', eq:true} would be exempted; requiring `locked` ties the exemption to the edge frozen at approval. It is a validation rule rather than a locking rule, because locking these edges would silently shadow spliced nodes."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_cursor_rename_fails_closed", "label": "A missing cursor node fails closed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A cursor node absent from the patched graph is not 'nothing to check' \u2014 it is the patch erasing the identity the positional check anchors to. Rename the node the run stands on (same shape, nothing locked touched) and a permissive guard skips positional dominance entirely; structural dominance cannot catch it because renaming a mid-graph node leaves every path from start intact."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_pure_patch_no_aliasing", "label": "applyPatchTo is pure and deep-clones patch values", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A shallow merge leaves the returned graph aliasing the caller's patch object, so a caller mutating that object later silently mutates an already-approved graph without it passing back through validateGraph. Non-array patch fields are ignored rather than iterated character-by-character. Removals run before updates before additions so a patch can replace a node id without colliding with itself."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_fnv1a_drift_detector", "label": "lockedHash FNV-1a is a drift detector, not a security boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pure JS because the conductor layer has no crypto; it catches a replanner quietly rewriting a locked gate, not an adversary hunting collisions. DoD checkSha uses real sha256 computed by a worker, which has full tools. stableStringify makes the fingerprint depend on content, not property order."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_fixture_must_match_shipping_shape", "label": "A test fixture must have the same shape as what ships", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only a gate's PASSING edge is locked in the seeds, so locking failure edges in the fixture too would make it over-locked: a test targeting the non-passing-edge rule could then pass via a LOCK violation instead, staying green even if the rule it exists to guard regressed."}, {"id": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_dead_end_and_orphan_rejection", "label": "Dead-end and orphan nodes rejected before the run starts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A reachable non-terminal node with no outgoing edge would make the interpreter throw on arrival; validateGraph catches it statically, and bails out early on a broken skeleton rather than piling confusing secondary errors on it."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_plan", "target": "docs_specs_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_design_loom", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_plan", "target": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_graph_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_plan", "target": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_scaffold_loom", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_plan", "target": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_test_loom", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_scaffold_loom", "target": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_graph_core", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_scaffold_loom", "target": "claude_never_hand_edit_generated_script", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_2026_07_27_loom_graph_runtime_test_loom", "target": "claude_conductor_layer_purity", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/2026-07-27-loom-graph-runtime.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "d